## Event [/api/event/{id}]
Manipulation of an individual event. It may be nicer to route based on the
event name instead of the event id.

+ Parameters
    + id (required, number, `1`) ... Numeric `id` of the Character to perform action with. Has example value.

### List an Event [GET]
Get details about the event denoted by {id}.

+ Response 200

    + Header

            X-My-Header : The Value

    + Body
    
            {"event_id" : 1,
            "event_name" : "The Battle of Blackwater Bay",
            "event_type" : "battle",
            "location_id" : 7,
            "event_description" : "The Battle of the Blackwater is the largest battle in the War of the Five Kings. The battle is fought between forces loyal to Stannis Baratheon and those loyal to Joffrey Baratheon. Stannis's army is on the verge of winning a decisive victory by defeating the rather large garrison of King's Landing, but is taken by surprise and all but annihilated by the joint forces of Tywin Lannister and the Tyrells."}
            }
            
+ Response 404 (application/json)

    + Header

            X-My-Header: The Value

    + Body

            {"message":"error", "errors":["not found"]}

## Location Collection [/api/locations]
Methods to manipulate the locations collection.
Again, this may be best parameterized if/when there are many events.

